-- title:
--   Tower and fine uniformisations agree through the degeneracy map d₀
-- statement:
--   The data are those of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of a quaternionic moduli tower at the prime $r$, together with a package of compatibility clauses; the conclusion is a single identity of $B$-points of the coarse space $\mathcal X$.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** Two distinct primes $r$, $\bar r$ and a non-zero squarefree integer $N$ divisible by neither.
--
--   **Base rings (`hdvr`, `hπ`, `hcomplete`, `hres`, `hunr`).** $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain with irreducible element $\pi$, $\pi$-adically complete, with residue ring of cardinality $r$ and with $(r)=(\pi)$; $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Further, $Onr$ is a characteristic-zero $\mathcal O$-algebra which is a domain, carrying an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, which ideal is maximal; `hOnr_alg` and `hOnr_closed` say that modulo this ideal every element is a root of a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ and every monic polynomial of positive degree has a root, and `hFr` says $Fr(x)\equiv x^{r}$ modulo it. The homomorphism $vdet\colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) is pinned down by `hvdet`: $vdet\,g=n$ exactly when $\det g=u\,\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Quaternionic data (`hB`, `hΛ`).** Rationals $a,b$ such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ satisfies $0<a$ or $0<b$ and is a division algebra at exactly the two finite places $r$ and $\bar r$, and $\Lambda$ a maximal order in it; `hΛℤ` says all rational integers lie in $\Lambda$.
--
--   **Moduli spaces.** $\mathcal X\to \mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal O$ with a point assignment $pt$ on fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level $N$, and `h𝒳` asserting that this is a coarse moduli datum (invariance under isomorphism, pullback compatibility, bijectivity on geometric points over algebraically closed fields, and the universal property). For a level $n\ge 3$ coprime to $r$, $\bar r$ and $N$, a scheme $M\to\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal O$ with $ptF$ on curves with full level-$n$ structure is a fine moduli datum (`hM`), and a group $G$ acts on $M$ by $\rho$ with labels $\chi\colon G\to\Lambda$ as a level-twist action (`hρ`: the automorphisms lie over the base, twisting a level structure by $\chi(g)$ realises $\rho(g)$ on points, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, injective and surjective modulo $n$). The forgetful morphism $p\colon M\to\mathcal X$ satisfies $p$ followed by $f$ equal to $fM$ (`hp`), is invariant under $\rho$ (`hρp`), and carries $ptF$-points to $pt$-points (`hp_pt`).
--
--   **The tower (`h𝒴`, `hd₀`, `hd₁`).** For each prime $\ell$ different from $r$ and $\bar r$, a scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal O$ with point assignment $ptT_\ell$ on curves carrying an extra level-$\ell$ subgroup scheme, coarse in the same sense, together with two morphisms $d_0(\ell),d_1(\ell)\colon\mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`): $d_0(\ell)$ sends the point of $(E,C)$ to the point of $E$, and $d_1(\ell)$ sends it to the point of any curve $d$ related to $(E,C)$ by a level-$\ell$ isogeny. Two endomorphisms $ar$, $arbar$ of $\mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ realise the Atkin–Lehner correspondences at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **The definite side (`hdef`, `hΛ₁`, `hR₁`, `hRΛ₁`, `hn₁`, `hS₁`, `hι₀`, `hv`).** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ ramified exactly at $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$ and an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ contained in it; an idele $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ such that $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$; an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\iota_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$; and the height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ above $r$. The group $\Gamma t$ is characterised by `hΓt` as the group of units of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ lying in the local unit boxes of $R_1$ at every place other than $v$. For each tower prime $\ell$, elements $s_\ell$ and ideles $sf_\ell$ satisfy `hs` (four clauses: $sf_\ell$ has component $s_\ell$ away from $r$, component $1$ at $r$, the product of the diagonal idele of $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set or the prime Hecke set of $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ according as $\ell\mid N$ or not, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$), and $\Gamma t_\ell$ is the intersection of $\Gamma t$ with its conjugate by $s_\ell$ (`hΓtℓ`). An element $wbar$ has reduced norm $\bar r$ and normalises $\Gamma t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **The special fibre.** A coordinate map $coord$ on $\Lambda$ with values in pairs of Witt vectors over $\mathbb F_{r^2}$ satisfying `hcoord` (additive, sending $1$ to $(1,0)$, multiplicative in the twisted sense, injective, with dense image and compatible with traces); a fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $Onr/(\pi)$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ along the unit section of $A_0$, and `hA₀` identifying the formal group of $A_0$ with $X_0$ via $coord$ and $\theta_0$.
--
--   **Endomorphisms of $A_0$.** Families $e,e'$ indexed by $\Gamma t$ with degrees $deg$ lying over the base (`he`), subject to `hE1` (each pair is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level-$N$ structure), `hE1mul` (multiplicativity up to multiplication by powers of $r$), `hE1sc` and `hE1'` (scalar elements of $\Gamma t$ correspond to multiplications, and conversely), `hE2` (for every injective ring map $E_0$ of the centraliser of the $X_0$-action into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g$ with each $e_\gamma$ induced on formal coordinates by an element $\varepsilon$ whose image is $r^{k_\gamma}g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$), `hE3` (labels in $\Lambda$ describing the effect of $e_\gamma$ on a full level-$n$ structure, multiplicative and compatible with scalars modulo $n$), and `hE4` (over algebraically closed fields every level-preserving $r$-power isogeny of a curve pulled back from $A_0$ comes from some $e_\gamma$ up to powers of $r$). Orders $R_2\le R_1$ and $R_2'\le\Lambda_{1s}$ with $r$-power denominators carry further endomorphism families $\hat e$, $\hat e'$ of $A_0$ over the base, subject to `hE5a`–`hE5e`, `hE5g` and `hE6a`–`hE6f` (compatibility with the group law, with the $\Lambda$-action and the level structure, multiplicativity, behaviour of units and of integers, the involution, comparison with the $e_\gamma$, matching with $\iota_0$ on formal coordinates, injectivity of $\hat e'$, and a divisibility clause at primes $q\ne r$); here $\Lambda_{1s}$ is a maximal order with $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_{1s}=R_1$ and $R_2\le R_2'$.
--
--   **The Drinfeld side.** A ring map $\iota$ from the Witt vectors of $\mathbb F_{r^2}$ to $Onr$; a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $Onr/(r)$ which is special for the induced structure map (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); a moduli package $MD$ over $Onr$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`); a comparison $\eta$ from rigidified objects to $MD$ satisfying `hη` (three clauses: over Noetherian bases $\eta$ separates admissible rigidified objects exactly up to isomorphism, it is natural in the base, and every point of $MD$ is locally in its image); and an injective $E_0$ on the centraliser of $\Phi$ with `hE₀` bounding it integrally by a fixed power of $r$ in both directions. The maps $eD$ realise an isomorphism of the functor of $MD$-points with the product of $\mathrm{Hom}_{\mathcal O}(Onr,-)$ and Drinfeld's functor of Deligne data $\Omega$, through `hnatD` (naturality), `hbijD` (bijectivity over Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent bases), `hfstD` (the first component is the structure map $\psi$), `hGLD` (the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action on $MD$-points corresponds to the $vdet$-twisted action on pairs), `hPiD` and `hPiexD` ($\pi$-translates exist and act by one Frobenius twist on the first component). In addition $\kappa$ with `hκ` reduces $Onr/(\pi)$ to $Onr/(r)$, and $\beta_0$ is an isogeny from $\Phi$ to the reduction of $X_0$ of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`). A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$ is fixed.
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner and Hecke data on $A_0$.** A curve $A_{0w}$ with morphisms $aw,aw',bw,bw'$ over the base realising the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (`hALw`) and an $r^{k_w}$-isogeny pair preserving the level (`hBSw`, `hBSwlev`), with `hJOINTw` matching simultaneously the $e_\gamma$ with $\iota_0(\gamma)$ and $aw$ followed by $bw$ with $\iota_0(wbar)$ on formal coordinates. Likewise, for each tower prime $\ell$, an extra level structure $C_0(\ell)$ on $A_0$, a curve $A_{0s}(\ell)$ with $as,as',bs,bs'$ realising the level-$\ell$ isogeny (`hLIs`) and an $r^{k_s}$-isogeny pair preserving the level (`hBSs`, `hBSslev`), with `hJOINTs` matching $as$ followed by $bs$ with $\iota_0(\overline{s_\ell})$; `hSTAB` states that $e_\gamma$ preserves $C_0(\ell)$ precisely when $\gamma\in\Gamma t_\ell$.
--
--   **The comparison $\Xi$ and its clauses.** $\Xi$ assigns to a rigidified curve over a Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebra a point of $MD$, subject to `hΞleg` (on connected bases its structure map is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (naturality under pullback of curves and rigidifications), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms compatible with the rigidifications up to powers of $r$) and `hΞdef` (an explicit description through $\eta$, rigidified transport along $\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0$ and admissibility, with twisting exponent $j\le 1$). With a normalising matrix $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, the clauses `heqΓ`, `heqW` and `heqS` assert that translating a rigidification by $e_\gamma$, by the Atkin–Lehner datum at $\bar r$, and by a level-$\ell$ isogeny corresponds, up to a power of the scalar $r$, to acting on $MD$-points by $g_0\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g_0^{-1}$, by $g_0\,\iota_0(wbar)\,g_0^{-1}$ and by $g_0\,\iota_0(\ell s^{-1})\,g_0^{-1}$ respectively; `heqS` carries its own copies of the Hecke hypotheses on $n_1$, $s$, $sf$ and of the joint matching clause.
--
--   **The uniformisations.** A group homomorphism $\theta t\colon\Gamma t\to G$ and a family $\Theta f$ sending, over a $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$, a triple consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $Onr\to B$, a Deligne datum over $B$ and an element of $G$, to a $B$-point of $M$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal O$, subject to: `hnat` (naturality in $B$), `hG` (right translation in $G$ corresponds to the automorphisms $\rho$), `hi'` ($\Gamma t$-invariance: twisted action by $\iota_0(\gamma)$ is absorbed by multiplying the $G$-coordinate by $\theta t(\gamma)$), `het` (unique lifting along surjections with square-zero-type kernels), `hfib` (the fibres of $\Theta f$ over algebraically closed fields are exactly the $\Gamma t$-orbits, described by $\theta t$, by pullback of Deligne data along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$ and by the Frobenius twist of $\psi$ by $-vdet(\iota_0(\gamma))$), `hC0e`, `hC0u` (existence and essential uniqueness of a normalised level-$n$ structure attached to a rigidification), `hC1e`, `hC1u`, `hC1p` (existence, uniqueness up to a compatible isomorphism, and pullback of the rigidified curve attached to a pair $(\psi,P)$ through $g_0^{-1}$), `hC2` and `hC2c` (the value clauses: the $M$-point $\Theta f(( \psi,P),1)$ is the $ptF$-point of the curve with its normalised level structure, and followed by $p$ it is the $pt$-point of that curve), `hC3`, `hC4`, `hC4pi` (the effect of the $\Gamma t$-action, of a general $\mathrm{GL}_2$-element and of a $\pi$-translate on the attached curves, level structures and extra level structures) and `hC5` (over algebraically closed fields, an isomorphism of two attached curves is matched by some $\gamma\in\Gamma t$, which twists the normalised level structures by $\chi(\theta t(\gamma))$ and for which, at one tower prime at a time, compatibility of extra level-$\ell$ structures is equivalent to stability of the corresponding extra level structure on $A_0$ under $e_\gamma$). Extra level structures are supplied and compared by `hCLe` and `hCLu`. Finally, for each tower prime $\ell$ a family $\Theta T_\ell$ sends a pair $(\psi,P)$ over a Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent $B$ to a $B$-point of $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\mathcal O$, natural in $B$ (`hnatT`), and `hVT` is the corresponding value clause: whenever the rigidified curve attached to $(\psi,P)$ through $g_0^{-1}$ carries an extra level-$\ell$ structure $C$ whose reduction is compatible with $C_0(\ell)$, the point $\Theta T_\ell(\psi,P)$ is the $ptT_\ell$-point of $(E,C)$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every prime $\ell$ different from $r$ and $\bar r$, every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, and every pair $x$ consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $Onr\to B$ and a Deligne datum over $B$, the $B$-point $\Theta T_\ell(x)$ of $\mathcal Y_\ell$ followed by $d_0(\ell)$ equals the $B$-point $\Theta f(x,1)$ of $M$ followed by $p$, as $B$-points of $\mathcal X$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal O$.
--
--   This is the compatibility clause of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation package which says that the tower uniformisations $\Theta T_\ell$ lie over the fine-level uniformisation $\Theta f$ through the first degeneracy map $d_0(\ell)$, the map that forgets the extra level-$\ell$ subgroup. It is used in the construction of the uniformised tower family attached to a fine moduli datum, in the edition in which the curve-isomorphism clause `hC5` is formulated one tower prime at a time.
